<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shahr Yagil Yuhargib</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shahr Yagil Yuhargib was a king of Qataban, an ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-arabia">South Arabian</a> kingdom with its capital at Timna in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a>. He is known from inscriptions in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qatabanian-language">Qatabanic</a> language, which record building works and royal decrees. Qataban grew rich from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/incense">incense</a> trade in frankincense and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/myrrh">myrrh</a> before it was absorbed by its neighbours, Hadramawt and Himyar.</p></div>
